1
00:00:20,067 --> 00:00:25,469
[SPEAKER_01]: So, this is a group of suttas that are basically on the same... talking about the same topic.

2
00:00:25,569 --> 00:00:28,809
[SPEAKER_01]: The first one is Angatranikāya, book of fives, number 151.

3
00:00:28,829 --> 00:00:40,673
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it says, because someone with five qualities isn't able to enter the sure path in regard to beneficial qualities, even when listening to the true teaching.

4
00:00:40,693 --> 00:00:41,173
[SPEAKER_01]: What five?

5
00:00:42,093 --> 00:00:45,254
[SPEAKER_01]: They discredit the talk, the speaker, or themselves.

6
00:00:46,153 --> 00:00:54,695
[SPEAKER_01]: They listen with a scattered and distracted mind, and they attend not through the origin, which is ayoniso, manasikāra.

7
00:00:55,715 --> 00:01:03,116
[SPEAKER_01]: Someone with these five qualities is unable to enter the sure path in regard to beneficial qualities, even when listening through teaching.

8
00:01:03,136 --> 00:01:11,277
[SPEAKER_01]: And it says, eh... someone with five qualities is able to enter the sure path in regard to beneficial qualities, when they have the opposite qualities.

9
00:01:11,317 --> 00:01:14,418
[SPEAKER_01]: So, they don't discredit the talk, eh... the speaker or themselves.

10
00:01:15,043 --> 00:01:20,105
[SPEAKER_01]: They listen with an unscattered and unified mind, and they attend through the origin.

11
00:01:20,245 --> 00:01:21,486
[SPEAKER_01]: So, yonisona-sikāra.

12
00:01:23,247 --> 00:01:23,807
[SPEAKER_01]: And, eh...

13
00:01:26,128 --> 00:01:36,333
[SPEAKER_01]: So, maybe we can start with that one, because the other two have sort of a similar structure, but those five things are slightly varied.

14
00:01:36,613 --> 00:01:41,135
[SPEAKER_01]: So, yeah.

